{"type":"standard","title":"Dan Ahlers","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Dan Ahlers</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q5216369","titles":{"canonical":"Dan_Ahlers","normalized":"Dan Ahlers","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Dan Ahlers</span></span>"},"pageid":17578916,"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1367747965","tid":"90278dec-905f-11f1-8a45-f9ea1c5b8458","timestamp":"2026-08-04T23:52:34Z","description":"American businessman and politician","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Ahlers","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Ahlers?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Ahlers?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Dan_Ahlers"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Ahlers","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Dan_Ahlers","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dan_Ahlers?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Dan_Ahlers"}},"extract":"Daniel Paul Ahlers is an American businessman and politician who served in both the South Dakota House of Representatives, from 2006 to 2008 and later from 2017 to 2019, and the South Dakota Senate, from 2008 to 2010. A member of the Democratic Party, Ahler represented the 25th legislative district, which encompasses Dell Rapids and areas north and northeast of Sioux Falls.","extract_html":"<p><b>Daniel Paul Ahlers</b> is an American businessman and politician who served in both the South Dakota House of Representatives, from 2006 to 2008 and later from 2017 to 2019, and the South Dakota Senate, from 2008 to 2010. A member of the Democratic Party, Ahler represented the 25th legislative district, which encompasses Dell Rapids and areas north and northeast of Sioux Falls.</p>"}